THIRD-PARTY SOURCE
The method SOPs (TM-104, TM-105) are adapted from:
Bringans S, Ito J, Casey T, et al. "A robust multiplex immunoaffinity mass
spectrometry assay (PromarkerD) for clinical prediction of diabetic kidney
disease." Clin Proteomics 2020;17:37. doi:10.1186/s12014-020-09302-w.
Licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
The methods were restructured and rewritten as controlled procedures for a
fictitious company; procedural detail was added for training purposes. The
authors, Proteomics International and Atturos do not endorse this work.
Anyone reusing the method SOPs must keep this attribution.

NOT LICENSED
- CC BY 4.0 covers the paper's text only. Neither this repository nor its
  licences grant any right to the biomarker patent or to the PromarkerD
  trade mark; the SOPs use the neutral name "3-plex immuno-MRM DKD assay".
- Positive Climb Diagnostics is a fictitious manufacturer. Names and roles in
  the SOPs are illustrative. The SOPs are training material: not a real
  company, product, QMS or validated laboratory procedure, and not for use
  in diagnostics or patient care.

